REVIEWER_VOTES: {novelty_killer: "API_ERROR — no vote received", systems_reviewer: yellow, evaluation_prosecutor: yellow, theory_skeptic: yellow, product_realist: yellow}
FATAL_OBJECTIONS: []
REQUIRED_EVIDENCE: [
  "L1 on real LMs (Llama-3.1-8B / Qwen2.5-7B) with real constrained backends (Outlines / XGrammar / vLLM guided JSON) on BFCL/ToolBench OOS slices — this is where ALL empirical weight now falls",
  "Unconstrained counterfactual baseline (evaluation_prosecutor): paired A/B on identical OOS prompts with and without hard grammar mask — if the unconstrained model also emits the near-miss tool, the constraint is not the causal culprit",
  "Semantic monitor baseline (evaluation_prosecutor): LLM-as-judge / reflection recall on the misrouted outputs — monitorability collapse currently only defeats syntactic validators, which are trivially blind by definition",
  "Real-LM logit monotonicity check (theory_skeptic): verify that real LM logits over tool-name tokens are actually monotone in semantic distance — without this the (K, neighbor-gap) law has no empirical anchor beyond the geometric proxy",
  "Novelty_killer prior-art search must be completed — API error means the dedicated novelty assessment is missing; cannot confirm no prior work articulates support-removal coercion + monitorability collapse in constrained decoding"
]
MANDATORY_BASELINES: [
  "Unconstrained generation on the same OOS prompts (isolate constraint-induced coercion from base-model parametric confusion)",
  "Semantic monitor / reflection-based detector (defeat a non-trivial monitor, not just a schema parser)",
  "Real-LM abstention/refusal rate without the grammar mask (what does instruction-tuned RLHF abstention buy before the mask erases it?)"
]
MAP_DELTA_PROPOSAL: {node: "CLAIM-0055", change: "status HELD/support -> YELLOW/pending-L1; add annotation: L0 establishes definitions and structural bounds, not behavioral predictions — theory_skeptic showed R1/R3/R4 are mathematical identities of the setup and R2/R5 are generic softmax algebra; conceptual novelty (support-removal as GAD-irrecoverable failure class + monitorability framing) is the surviving load-bearing contribution; L1 MUST include unconstrained baseline + semantic monitor + logit-monotonicity check to carry empirical weight"}
PRIOR_ART_ADEQUATE: no
RATIONALE: prompt_version=v001. Four of five reviewers voted YELLOW; the novelty_killer failed (API error), leaving the dedicated prior-art search incomplete — this alone blocks GREEN per standing rules.

The surviving contribution is CONCEPTUAL, not empirical. Theory_skeptic delivered the sharpest critique and it is unrebutted: (1) R1 is a tautology — stream-misroute = P(OOS) = (144−K)/144 matches the reported numbers to 3 decimals; the "kernel-independent geometric law" is independent of the kernel because it never references the kernel. (2) R3 (validity-monitor recall = 0) and R4 (GAD recovery = 0) are true by construction/definition — no experiment was needed; one line of probability gives both. (3) R2 and R5 are generic softmax-over-distance behavior. The L0 results CANNOT FAIL given the construction. There is no risky prediction the L0 could have falsified. "Kernel-independence is the signature of a tautology, not of a robust law" — this reframing is correct and the packet's "STRONGEST possible anti-tuned-knob result" framing inverts the diagnosis.

However, this does NOT kill the claim — it recategorizes it. The structural argument is sound and genuinely novel: (a) support-removal coercion as a named failure class that is by definition outside GAD's within-support recovery (theory_skeptic concurs this is "not in GAD or the abstention literature"); (b) the monitorability collapse framing (schema-validate + retry + GAD + escape-hatch all fail simultaneously) is a useful safety contribution even if each component follows from definitions; (c) the observation that "Wait that's not an option" (2409.00113) covers UNconstrained MCQ where the model retains the choice, while hard-constrained decoding REMOVES the choice, is a clean gap in the literature. Systems_reviewer confirms the substrate is real and dominant (vLLM, SGLang, TensorRT-LLM all implement hard grammar constraints). Product_realist confirms actionable guidance exists.

The evaluation_prosecutor's objections are the most consequential for L1 design: (i) without an unconstrained baseline, the claim "the decoder mechanically coerces" is ungrounded — if the base model also emits the near-miss without the mask (due to semantic priming from the tool prompt or parametric confusion), then the constraint is not the causal agent; (ii) claiming "monitorability collapse" while only testing a schema parser is a strawman — semantic monitors (reflection/LLM-as-judge) are the production-relevant adversary and are untested. Both must be addressed in L1 or the causal and monitorability claims are hollow.

YELLOW is the correct consensus. The claim advances to L1 with the explicit understanding that L0 established definitions and bounds, not behavior. The L1 must produce genuinely risky predictions: real-LM misroute rates that could falsify the (K, neighbor-gap) law on real logit geometry, an unconstrained baseline that could show the model already fails without the mask, and a semantic monitor that could break the monitorability collapse. If all three survive, GREEN. If the unconstrained model also misroutes, or real logits are non-monotone in tool-token distance, or a reflection step catches the near-miss — the claim's causal and safety framing collapses regardless of how clean the structural argument is.
